# No shared secret. On a tailnet the server authenticates each WebSocket upgrade
# with: 1. Origin (must match this server's host), 2. Sec-Fetch-Site (refuses
# cross-site), 3. tailscale whois (peer must be your own tailnet identity).
# On a laptop it runs in localhost mode — see below — serving this machine only.
#
# Bind address. Use the tailscale IP so tailnet devices can reach it.
# The server refuses 0.0.0.0 — /pty is an ungated shell.
CODETERM_HOST=100.64.0.1
CODETERM_PORT=8123

# ── Localhost mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run it on your own laptop instead of a tailnet box. With CODETERM_HOST set to
# a loopback address the server serves this machine only and needs no tailscale
# — a laptop with no tailnet just works. Set CODETERM_LOCALHOST=1 to force it
# even where tailscale is installed. A non-loopback bind still requires a
# tailnet identity; the server refuses to expose an ungated shell with no auth.
# CODETERM_HOST=127.0.0.1
# CODETERM_LOCALHOST=1


# Directory the agent works in.
CODETERM_WORKSPACE=/home/dev/projects/codeTerminal/workspace

# Extra hostnames you browse to, comma-separated (e.g. a /etc/hosts alias).
# Needed so the Origin check accepts them.
# CODETERM_ORIGINS=dev.hetzner

# CODETERM_DEBUG=1   # log every event emitted to the agent pane

# Allow the "Never ask" permission mode (bypassPermissions). Off by default:
# it lets the agent run Bash and edit files with nobody approving.
# CODETERM_ALLOW_BYPASS=1
